  "narrative": {
   "care_continuity": [
    "National isolation/CTE stock: 817. The source prints no complete national capacity denominator.",
    "Ituri: 495 patients for 978 beds (50.6%); Nord-Kivu: 237 for 220 beds (107.7%, oversaturated); Haut-Uele: 62 for 128 beds (48.4%); Tshopo: 7 for 25 beds (28.0%); Sud-Kivu: 16 for 25 beds (64.0%).",
    "Bas-Uele describes no normative CTE/CT or ambulance but publishes no occupancy block; its values remain unset rather than inferred."
   ],
   "challenges": [
    "Alert volume rebounded 19.6% (1 792 to 2 144) with all six provinces reporting and verification recovering to 91.2% (1 955/2 144). Across five cuts the series has swung -30.3%, +53.1%, -31.3%, +19.6% with no INSP correction to the completeness and time-window question SR109 raised. Treat it as a reporting-coverage artefact, not a transmission signal.",
    "PoE/PoC report completeness fell to 78.9%. Bas-Uele did not report, Tshopo sits at 83.3% (15/18) with only 12 of 30 planned PoC activated, and only 1 of 11 (9.1%) strategic Ituri points runs without interruption, with Avakubi still closed for security.",
    "Contact follow-up fell to 86.0% (21 909/25 500) from 88.5%. Haut-Uele dropped to 72.1% (1 215/1 685) and Bas-Uele to 69.7% (106/152). Sud-Kivu publishes no contact row. INSP attributes the weakness to insufficient teams dedicated to surveillance and contact follow-up.",
    "Care capacity: Nord-Kivu is oversaturated at 107.7% (237 patients, 220 beds) with some patients held in non-normative facilities. In Ituri the CME CTE is saturated for confirmed cases and the Nizi, Lita, Mambasa and Logo sites for suspects, with extension delayed at Nizi and Bambu. Bas-Uele still has no normative CTE/CT and no ambulance.",
    "A new health zone, Kayna in Nord-Kivu, is affected for the first time: 1 confirmed case, no deaths. The national footprint moves to 61 of 151 health zones.",
    "The page-one prose prints the 61/151 footprint as 40.3%. The sidebar and the printed Table 1 total both give 40.4%, which the arithmetic supports; the prose figure is a source rounding error."
   ],
   "highlights": [
    "DRC: 6522 confirmed and 3134 confirmed deaths.",
    "24h: 86 confirmations and 39 deaths (30 community, 9 intra-CTE).",
    "Footprint: 61/151 health zones across six provinces; Kayna is newly affected in Nord-Kivu.",
    "The 61/151 coverage is 40.4%; the page-one prose prints 40.3%, a source rounding error."
   ]
  },
